  "ref": "ISA.49.18",
  "review_notes": [
    "Rule 44's closing limit is what separates these from the adverbial accusatives of 49.23 and 49.26, where the supplied preposition stays with its noun: kullam and the suffix on tqashsherim are the verbs' own objects, appayim and damam are not.",
    "The competing reading, leaving with on the demoted object nominal, is what the verse pass took; it is set aside because rule 44 places a preposition supplied for a direct object by the English verb's valency and the chapter reads it that way in five other verses."
  ]
